IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Land Authority Act 2001 (Singapore) -- what "State land" is (s 2), the Authority's power to demand land information
-- and the offences around it (s 8), personal immunity (s 12), borrowing (s 20), the financial year (s 21), misuse of the
-- Authority's symbol (s 30), enforcement powers and the Third Schedule laws they reach (s 31, Third Schedule), liability of
-- officers and partners (s 32), composition (s 33), secrecy (s 35), and the board's size, quorum, voting and vacancies (s 5,
-- First Schedule paras 7, 9, 11, 13).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SLAA2001.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 42 of 2022 (in force 1 November 2024) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. It is an institutional Act: it sets up the
-- Authority that runs land registration, survey and State land. SCOPED to the rules with decision content. Not encoded: the
-- functions list (s 6, which s 6(4) makes unenforceable in court), the general powers (s 7), Ministerial directions (s 9),
-- committees and delegation (s 10), staff (s 11), funds and application of moneys (ss 14, 15), estimates (s 17), investment
-- (s 18), grants (s 19), shares (s 20A), proceedings by officers (s 34), rules (s 36), references in other law (s 37), and the
-- substance of the Third Schedule laws themselves.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Land Authority Act 2001`

§§ `2 -- State land`

-- s 2: "State land" means all land in Singapore EXCEPT (a) land "lawfully granted, or contracted to be granted, in fee simple or
-- estate in perpetuity" by the Government; (b) land "subject to any agreement, lease or licence lawfully granted" by the
-- Government; and (c) land "dedicated as national parks or nature reserves", AND "includes any land which, having been granted or
-- held under any agreement, lease or licence, has been lawfully surrendered or resumed or compulsorily acquired", and land
-- "lawfully forfeited to, or by any means has reverted ... to, the Government".
-- READING (an inference): the "includes" limb is taken to bring land back in even where a past grant or lease would otherwise
-- exclude it. A national park or nature reserve is OUTSIDE State land on this definition.
DECLARE Land HAS
    `granted in fee simple or in perpetuity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `subject to a Government agreement, lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dedicated as a national park or nature reserve` IS A BOOLEAN
    `surrendered, resumed or compulsorily acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `forfeited or reverted to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the land` IS A Land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is State land` IF
        `the land`'s `surrendered, resumed or compulsorily acquired`
    OR  `the land`'s `forfeited or reverted to the Government`
    OR  (     (NOT `the land`'s `granted in fee simple or in perpetuity`)
          AND (NOT `the land`'s `subject to a Government agreement, lease or licence`)
          AND (NOT `the land`'s `dedicated as a national park or nature reserve`))

§§ `8 -- requests for land information`

-- s 8(1): the Authority may request "any person" to provide information on land tenure, transactions, ownership, boundaries or
-- other geographical information. (2) the request "must be in writing", "must be served", and "must specify the particulars".
-- (3) an offence: (a) "wilfully refuses or without lawful excuse (the proof of which lies on the person) neglects" to provide the
-- information in the time, form or place specified; or (b) "wilfully provides ... any false information". Fine up to $1,000 and,
-- for a continuing offence, "a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day" after conviction.
-- (4) nothing obliges a person to provide information "not in the person's possession or which the person is prohibited by law
-- from disclosing".
-- READING: s 8(4) is taken to answer a charge of refusing or neglecting, but not one of giving false information.
DECLARE InformationRequest HAS
    `in writing, served and specifying the information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wilfully refused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `neglected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wilfully gave false information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was not held or disclosure was prohibited by law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the request` IS AN InformationRequest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8 is committed` IF
        `the request`'s `in writing, served and specifying the information`
    AND (    (     (NOT `the request`'s `the information was not held or disclosure was prohibited by law`)
               AND (    `the request`'s `wilfully refused`
                    OR  (`the request`'s `neglected` AND (NOT `the request`'s `proved a lawful excuse`))))
         OR  `the request`'s `wilfully gave false information`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 8` MEANS
    1000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `Penalties -- ss 8, 30, 31, 35`

-- s 8(3): fine $1,000 (no imprisonment). s 30(2): fine $5,000 or 6 months or both. s 31(2): fine $10,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 35(2): fine $2,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to provide land information`
    `misusing the Authority's symbol`
    `obstructing an Authority officer`
    `disclosing Authority information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to provide land information` THEN 1000
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing an Authority officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `disclosing Authority information` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to provide land information` THEN 0
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing an Authority officer` THEN 6
    WHEN `disclosing Authority information` THEN 12

§§ `12 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 12(1): no suit lies personally against a member, officer, employee or person acting under the Authority's direction "for
-- anything which is in good faith and with reasonable care done or omitted" in the execution or purported execution of this Act or
-- any other written law. (2): where the Authority supplies information to the public under written law, neither it nor its people
-- are liable for loss from "any error or omission" if made "in good faith and in the ordinary course" of duties.
GIVEN `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN, `in executing written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is personally immune` IF
    `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care` AND `in executing written law`

GIVEN `information supplied to the public under written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `error made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is not liable for the information error` IF
    `information supplied to the public under written law` AND `error made in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `20 -- borrowing`

-- s 20: the Authority "may raise loans from the Government or, with the approval of the Minister for Finance, raise loans from
-- banks or other financial institutions (whether in Singapore or elsewhere)".
-- INFERENCE: s 20 names no other lender, so borrowing from anyone else is taken as not authorised by s 20.
DECLARE Lender IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a Singapore bank`
    `a foreign financial institution`
    `a private individual`

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender, `the Minister for Finance approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan is authorised by section 20` IF
    CONSIDER `the lender`
    WHEN `the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore bank` THEN `the Minister for Finance approved`
    WHEN `a foreign financial institution` THEN `the Minister for Finance approved`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `21 -- financial year`

-- s 21: the financial year "begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year".
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year begins in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

§§ `30 -- the Authority's symbol`

-- s 30(2): an offence to use a symbol "identical with that of the Authority or which so resembles" it "as to deceive or cause
-- confusion, or to be likely to deceive or cause confusion". No defence or intent element is stated.
GIVEN `identical` IS A BOOLEAN, `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of the symbol is an offence` IF
    `identical` OR `resembles it so as to be likely to deceive or confuse`

§§ `31 and Third Schedule -- enforcement`

-- s 31(1): an officer or employee may, "in relation to any offence under this Act or any written law set out in the Third
-- Schedule", on "declaration of his or her office and production ... of the identification card", require identity, information
-- and documents, and attendance. (2): refusing access, obstructing, wilfully misstating, refusing information without lawful
-- excuse, or failing to comply with a lawful demand is an offence.
-- Third Schedule: 1. ss 8, 11, 20 Boundaries and Survey Maps Act 1998. 2. s 46 Land Acquisition Act 1966. 3. ss 7, 27, 59, 169
-- Land Titles Act 1993. 4. ss 7, 15, 37, 41, 42, 43, 49, 54, 62, 65, 66, 67, 81, 82, 111, 113, 120 Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967.
-- 5. ss 4, 9, 10, 11, 16, 23, 25, 35, 36 Residential Property Act 1976. 6. ss 5, 6, 10(2), 12(5), 18(5), 23(5) and (7), 24(3),
-- 26(1) and (2) State Lands Protection Act 2022. 7. all provisions of the Land Betterment Charge Act 2021.
-- Neither the State Lands Act 1920 nor the Registration of Deeds Act 1988 appears in the Schedule.
-- `subsection` is 0 where the provision is named as a whole section.
DECLARE LandLaw IS ONE OF
    `Boundaries and Survey Maps Act 1998`
    `Land Acquisition Act 1966`
    `Land Titles Act 1993`
    `Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967`
    `Residential Property Act 1976`
    `State Lands Protection Act 2022`
    `Land Betterment Charge Act 2021`
    `State Lands Act 1920`
    `Registration of Deeds Act 1988`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER, `c` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `n is one of four` IF
    `n` EQUALS `a` OR `n` EQUALS `b` OR `n` EQUALS `c` OR `n` EQUALS `d`

GIVEN `section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `strata section listed` IF
        `n is one of four` `section` 7 15 37 41
    OR  `n is one of four` `section` 42 43 49 54
    OR  `n is one of four` `section` 62 65 66 67
    OR  `n is one of four` `section` 81 82 111 113
    OR  `section` EQUALS 120

GIVEN `section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `residential property section listed` IF
        `n is one of four` `section` 4 9 10 11
    OR  `n is one of four` `section` 16 23 25 35
    OR  `section` EQUALS 36

GIVEN `section` IS A NUMBER, `subsection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `state lands protection provision listed` IF
        `section` EQUALS 5
    OR  `section` EQUALS 6
    OR  (`section` EQUALS 10 AND `subsection` EQUALS 2)
    OR  (`section` EQUALS 12 AND `subsection` EQUALS 5)
    OR  (`section` EQUALS 18 AND `subsection` EQUALS 5)
    OR  (`section` EQUALS 23 AND (`subsection` EQUALS 5 OR `subsection` EQUALS 7))
    OR  (`section` EQUALS 24 AND `subsection` EQUALS 3)
    OR  (`section` EQUALS 26 AND (`subsection` EQUALS 1 OR `subsection` EQUALS 2))

GIVEN `the law` IS A LandLaw, `section` IS A NUMBER, `subsection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is in the Third Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `Boundaries and Survey Maps Act 1998` THEN `n is one of four` `section` 8 11 20 20
    WHEN `Land Acquisition Act 1966` THEN `section` EQUALS 46
    WHEN `Land Titles Act 1993` THEN `n is one of four` `section` 7 27 59 169
    WHEN `Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967` THEN `strata section listed` `section`
    WHEN `Residential Property Act 1976` THEN `residential property section listed` `section`
    WHEN `State Lands Protection Act 2022` THEN `state lands protection provision listed` `section` `subsection`
    WHEN `Land Betterment Charge Act 2021` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `offence under this Act or a Third Schedule provision` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared office and produced identification card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may exercise section 31 powers` IF
    `offence under this Act or a Third Schedule provision` AND `declared office and produced identification card`

§§ `32 -- officers and partners`

-- s 32(1): where a body corporate's offence was committed "with the consent or connivance of, or ... attributable to any neglect"
-- of a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, that person "as well as the body corporate" is guilty.
-- (5): where a partnership is guilty, "every partner, other than a partner who is proved to have been ignorant of or to have
-- attempted to prevent the commission of the offence, is also guilty".
GIVEN `the body corporate committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the officer's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the body corporate committed the offence` AND (`with the officer's consent or connivance` OR `attributable to the officer's neglect`)

GIVEN `the partnership is guilty` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved ignorant of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved attempted to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner is also guilty` IF
        `the partnership is guilty`
    AND (NOT `proved ignorant of the offence`)
    AND (NOT `proved attempted to prevent it`)

§§ `33 -- composition`

-- s 33(1): the Chief Executive or an officer authorised by the Chief Executive "may compound any offence under this Act which is
-- prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding $1,000". (2) on payment no further proceedings.
-- (3) sums go to the Consolidated Fund.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `by the Chief Executive or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is valid` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `by the Chief Executive or an authorised officer` AND `the sum` AT MOST 1000

§§ `35 -- secrecy`

-- s 35(1): a person "who is or has been" a member, officer, employee or agent of the Authority, or a member of a committee, "must
-- not disclose any information or matter relating to the affairs of the Authority or of any other person" obtained in performing
-- duties -- "Except for the purpose of the performance of his or her duties ... or when lawfully required to do so by any court or
-- where required or allowed by any written law". (2) fine $2,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `by a current or former member, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of information obtained in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for the purpose of performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 35` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `by a current or former member, officer, employee, agent or committee member`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `of information obtained in performing duties`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `for the purpose of performing duties`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by written law`)

§§ `5 and First Schedule -- the board`

-- s 5(1): a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson and "not less than 8 but not more than 20 other members".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board size complies with section 5` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 8 AND `other members` AT MOST 20

-- First Schedule para 13(2): "The quorum for a meeting of the Authority is half the number of its members."
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `present` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `members`

-- para 13(5): decisions "by a simple majority of the votes of the members present and voting"; on "an equality of votes" the
-- Chairperson (or Deputy, or the member presiding) "has a casting vote".
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is adopted` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `casting vote for`)

-- para 13(7): where "at least 4 members" request by "written notice signed by them", the Chairperson "must, within 7 days from the
-- receipt of the notice, convene a meeting".
GIVEN `members requesting` IS A NUMBER, `written notice signed by them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chairperson must convene a meeting` IF
    `members requesting` AT LEAST 4 AND `written notice signed by them`

GIVEN `day notice received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to convene` MEANS
    `day notice received` PLUS 7

-- para 7: a member "may resign ... at any time by giving at least one month's notice in writing to the Minister".
GIVEN `months of written notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation notice is sufficient` IF
    `months of written notice` AT LEAST 1

-- para 9: the office "becomes vacant" if the member (a) becomes disqualified; (b) "fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the
-- Authority without sufficient cause (the sufficiency thereof to be decided by the Authority)"; (c) resigns; or (d) dies.
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `the Authority found sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacated by absence` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `the Authority found sufficient cause`)

-- para 11: a person must not be appointed or continue in office if (a) incapacitated by illness; (b) "an undischarged bankrupt or has
-- made any arrangement or composition with his or her creditors"; (c) convicted of an offence of "dishonesty, fraud or moral
-- turpitude" without a free pardon; (d) "sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more" without a free pardon; or
-- (e) otherwise unable or unfit.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `incapacitated by illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `undischarged bankrupt or compounded with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `otherwise unable or unfit` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified` IF
        `the candidate`'s `incapacitated by illness`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `undischarged bankrupt or compounded with creditors`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `convicted of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `otherwise unable or unfit`
